                <pb facs="0634" n="510" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg510"/>

                <head>No. 309.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lowell to Mr. Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-03-09"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 9,
                        1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Interview with the minister for foreign affairs this afternoon. He says cabinet
                    equally desirous with Evarts to accelerate settlement. As Evarts did not see his
                    way to accept terms last offered, secretary is willing to consent to reference
                    either to you or late Secretary of State with British minister at Washington. Is
                    willing to pay £15,000 for all claims up to end of last year. If cruisers be
                    sent as intimated in 109, he would be glad to know your opinion of joint
                    cruisers with joint instructions.</p>
                <closer><signed>LOWELL.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
